package Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds

/*
A TerrainCollisionPiece is a small square of ground that the physics engine
can collide with, but that is never drawn. A TerrainCollision keeps a few of
them near the player, and moves them as the player moves, so only the
ground nearby costs anything in physics.

It is a TerrainPatch with no mesh, kept hidden. Its collision shape reads
the heights straight from the TerrainData.

This matches the collision shapes Terrain3DCollision makes in its dynamic
mode, which are 16 samples across by default.

Attribute: Example
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainData
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Worlds.TerrainCollisionPiece

TerrainData data
data:AddRegion(0, 0)
TerrainCollisionPiece piece
piece:Place(data, 32, 48, 16)
*/
class TerrainCollisionPiece is TerrainPatch
    on create
        // A piece only collides. It has no mesh, so it is never drawn.
        Hide()
        SetName("Terrain Collision Piece")
    end

    /*
    This action moves the piece to cover a square of samples, and gives it
    the collision shape for the ground there. Physics settings, such as
    friction, are kept. A piece that is in a game should be removed from it
    before being placed, and added again after, so the physics engine sees
    its new shape and position.

    Attribute: Parameter data The heights of the whole terrain.
    Attribute: Parameter firstX The square's first sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter firstZ The square's first sample along z.
    Attribute: Parameter size How many cells the square covers along each side.
    */
    action Place(TerrainData data, integer firstX, integer firstZ, integer size)
        Measure(data, firstX, firstZ, size)
        ApplyCollisionShape()
        PlaceInWorld()
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the piece covers the square starting at a
    sample.

    Attribute: Parameter firstX The square's first sample along x.
    Attribute: Parameter firstZ The square's first sample along z.
    Attribute: Returns True if the piece starts at that sample.
    */
    action Covers(integer firstX, integer firstZ) returns boolean
        return GetTerrainData() not= undefined and GetFirstSampleX() = firstX and GetFirstSampleZ() = firstZ
    end
end
